<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06FH">Remark <span data-tag="06FH">9.2.9.12</span>.</a> Let $\kappa \leq \lambda $ be regular cardinals and let $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a $(\kappa ,\lambda )$-cocomplete inner fibration of simplicial sets. Then the $\infty $-category of sections $\operatorname{Fun}_{/\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{E}})$ is $(\kappa ,\lambda )$-cocomplete. Moreover, for every object $C \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, the evaluation functor $\operatorname{ev}_{C}: \operatorname{Fun}_{/\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}) \rightarrow \operatorname{Fun}_{ / \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}( \{ C\} , \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}) = \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}_{C}$ is $(\kappa ,\lambda )$-finitary. By virtue of Remark <a data-tag="06FD" href="/tag/06FD">9.2.9.8</a>, this is a special case of Corollary <a data-tag="06AS" href="/tag/06AS">7.1.10.4</a>. </p>
</article>
